      "problem": "What is the supremum of the set $B=\\{-5,\\,4,\\,1,\\,0,\\,-3\\}?$\n\n$sup(B)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The supremum of a set $B$ is the smallest upper bound of $B.$\n\nIf $B$ is a finite set, the supremum of $B$ equals its maximum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sup(B) & =max\\{-5,\\,4,\\,1,\\,0,\\,-3\\}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
